<figure class="homeport-flow" aria-labelledby="homeport-flow-caption">
  <div class="flow-device"><strong>Your browser</strong><span>Send “Run the tests.”</span></div>
  <div class="flow-link"><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span> Private HTTPS · Tailscale Serve</div>
  <div class="flow-mini">
    <div class="flow-location">On the Mac mini</div>
    <ol class="flow-stages">
      <li><div><strong>Homeport web app</strong><span>Checks access. Accepts the request.</span></div><small>Pydantic validates <br /><code>Submission → Task</code></small></li>
      <li><div><strong>SQLite</strong><span>Saves the task before work starts.</span></div><small>Stores the prompt, <br />IDs, state, and results</small></li>
      <li><div><strong>Python worker</strong><span>Takes the next task. Starts or resumes its conversation.</span></div><small>Saves intent, then sends <br /><code>turn/start</code></small></li>
      <li class="flow-codex"><div><strong>Codex App Server</strong><span>Runs the agent. Uses tools. Maintains the conversation.</span></div><small>JSON-RPC over <br />a private Unix socket</small></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <div class="flow-link"><span aria-hidden="true">↕</span> Codex ↔ OpenAI · model requests</div>
  <div class="flow-device"><strong>OpenAI</strong><span>Runs model inference through Codex authentication.</span></div>
  <div class="flow-return"><strong>Return path: Homeport → browser</strong><span>Homeport reads Codex history and shows progress. The worker saves events and checked results.</span></div>
  <figcaption id="homeport-flow-caption">Pydantic runs inside Homeport’s Python code. It checks records at the data boundaries; it is not another service or another agent. The optional Codex terminal connects to the same App Server.</figcaption>
</figure>
